name: application-security
description: Reusable application security skill for code review, audit, exploitability analysis, authorization review, trust-boundary tracing, and evidence-based security reporting.
---

# Application Security

Use this skill when the request involves:
- security review
- audit
- vulnerability analysis
- exploitability analysis
- authorization or access control review
- source-to-sink tracing
- code-level AppSec triage

## Read Order

1. Read `<project>/AGENTS.md` if present.
2. Read the relevant project docs in `docs/` or `references/`.
3. Load `references/review-workflow.md` for the reusable workflow.
4. Only then start tracing data flow and evaluating defenses.

## Skill Responsibilities

- Provide a reusable AppSec workflow across projects
- Prioritize context over pattern matching
- Enforce evidence-based reporting and refutation
- Keep project-specific facts out of the skill itself

## Output Contract

- Every conclusion needs code references
- Every mature finding needs at least one refutation attempt
- Every severity needs a concrete "why not one level lower?"
- If proof is incomplete, use `UNCERTAIN` instead of overstating confidence

## Load On Demand

- Reusable workflow: `references/review-workflow.md`
- Project facts: `<project>/docs/*`

